      "text": "72-year-old female presenting with constipation for 5 months. Character: hard stool, passing once in 3 days; radiation: n/a; aggravated by less water intake; relieved by warm water. Severity 3/10. Associated: bloating. PMH: Coronary artery disease, stent 8 years ago. Drugs: Aspirin 75 mg; Atorvastatin 20 mg. Allergy: no known allergies. Family: no similar illness. Personal: non-smoker, no alcohol. Triage: ROUTINE."
